<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 24 March, from 1387 to 1976.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1387">1387 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">639 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard Fitzalan's English fleet attacks a wine fleet at Margate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the Caroline War phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, an English fleet under Richard Fitzalan, Earl of Arundel, attacked a wine fleet of 250 to 360 French, Flemish and Castilian vessels. The battle continued into the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1401">1401 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">625 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Timur sacks Damascus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Central Asian conqueror's army plundered and burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> after its surrender, and its craftsmen were carried off to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> survived, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> was devastated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1603">1603 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">423 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth I dies and James VI of Scotland inherits England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Elizabeth died at Richmond Palace, and her cousin James VI became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-vi-and-i">James I of England</a> and Ireland. The crowns were united, though the kingdoms stayed separate until 1707.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1765">1765 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">261 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parliament passes the Quartering Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The act required American colonies to provide barracks and supplies for British troops. Resentment of it was later listed among the grievances in the Declaration of Independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1794">1794 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tadeusz Kościuszko proclaims a general uprising in Kraków</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tadeusz-kosciuszko">Tadeusz Kościuszko</a> proclaimed a general uprising against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and took command of all Polish forces. His speech is considered the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosciuszko-uprising">Kościuszko Uprising</a>, whose defeat led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-partition-of-poland">Third Partition</a> of 1795.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosciuszko-uprising">Kościuszko Uprising</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tadeusz-kosciuszko">Tadeusz Kościuszko</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1882">1882 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">144 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Koch identifies the tuberculosis bacterium</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a lecture in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, Koch showed that tuberculosis, then causing about one in seven deaths in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, was caused by a bacterium. 24 March is now World Tuberculosis Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied prisoners break out in the 'Great Escape'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">That night 76 airmen crawled through a tunnel out of Stalag Luft III in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagan">Sagan</a>. Only three reached safety; on Hitler's orders, 50 of those recaptured were shot.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/isabel-peron" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isabel-peron.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1976">1976 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">50 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Military coup overthrows Isabel Perón in Argentina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A junta led by General Jorge Videla took power and began the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dirty-war">Dirty War</a>'. Thousands of people, estimated at up to 30,000, were 'disappeared' before military rule ended in 1983.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 24 March <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yue-fei"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yue-fei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Yue Fei</span><span class="tp">1103–1142</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georgius-agricola"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georgius-agricola.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georgius Agricola</span><span class="tp">1494–1555</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/michiel-de-ruyter"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michiel-de-ruyter.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Michiel de Ruyter</span><span class="tp">1607–1676</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vojislav-kostunica"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vojislav-kostunica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vojislav Koštunica</span><span class="tp">b. 1944</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 24 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wulfred"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wulfred.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wulfred</span><span class="tp">d. 832</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hosokawa-harumoto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hosokawa-harumoto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hosokawa Harumoto</span><span class="tp">1514–1563</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elizabeth-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Elizabeth I</span><span class="tp">1533–1603</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/oscar-romero"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oscar-romero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Óscar Romero</span><span class="tp">1917–1980</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sir-john-kerr"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sir-john-kerr.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sir John Kerr</span><span class="tp">1914–1991</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cesar-milstein"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cesar-milstein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">César Milstein</span><span class="tp">1927–2002</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
